WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
I was expecting to see, you know, like,
as always, some of the brothers have a good time.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Walk into the ZBT house and the first thing you hear
is like boom boom boom. You hear that music.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.000
And my heart beats through music, I can't lie.
I'm an Orthodox Jew, so I keep Shabbat, I keep kosher.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.000
And Judaism is kind of part of my everyday life.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Shabbat starts at sundown on Friday,
so I get dressed up for dinner.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.000
I go over to Chabad, help set up. We have dinner,
then I head back home, sleep, wake up in the morning—

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.000
and go to services.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.000
We have a beautiful meal filled with
over 100 Jewish students on campus.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Right across the street from our friends over at ZBT.
So Max and I have this friend named Rand.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.000
My name is Rand. And he's an amazing guy.
But unfortunately, he's been stricken with tough times recently.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
So we want to go console him on a Saturday afternoon.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.000
It's like maybe 1 or 2 p.m. We're a little bored.
It's Shabbat. We don't have our phones.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.000
So we're looking for something to do.
We decide, hey, let's go see Randy.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.000
There was some event going on, but I wasn't really sure.
I was a little hesitant, but not really.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Basically, we kind of walked up
to the front door of the ZBT house.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Trying to see Rand, just calm him down
from whatever kind of trauma he has.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:41.000
And then some person ran out in a bikini from the side,
and seemed to know Max, was like, "Hey, guys, come on over."

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:47.000
We see this other friend, Sophia, and she says,
"Max, Benjamin, you guys, come around the back."

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:53.000
And I'm like, "Okay, you know, Sophia,
she's a great girl. We trust her."

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.000
I noticed afterwards, apparently, it's not normal
for guys to just walk into a frat party.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:08.000
They're usually pretty fine.
A couple pointing fingers. I don't judge.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:14.000
They don't charge us, we don't charge them. That works.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.000
There were groups of people that you could see pointing at us.
We are Jewish — but at an event like this—

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Everyone's wearing wildly different clothing,
and I just saw these two guys staring up at me.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.000
We came to support a friend. And we ended up having,
for us at least, a once-in-a-lifetime experience.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:38.000
We laughed with more friends than we came with,
and that's always a good thing.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:44.000
When the ZBT guys saw me,
they welcomed me with open arms.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Did anything make you uncomfortable?
No. I mean, yeah.
